    "label": "Apply an amount across rows of another list",
    "job": "Work out how the amount one row holds (a payment, a credit, a grant) goes across the open amounts of rows of another list (invoices, bills, budgets) as allocation rows, propose it first, answer allocations to take back, or read what is applied and open on a row",
    "description": "action propose works out, writing nothing, how the source row's amount would go across the targets in an order (oldest_first by default, or as read-data/list-settlements.json orders say) and what is left unapplied as a credit. apply answers one allocation row per target (source, target, amount, date, request) for the allocations list \"<source>-to-<target>-allocations\" under `keep`, for the caller to store; give items [{ target_id, amount }] or leave them out to apply the proposal; request_key makes it apply once. Every item is answered done, already_done or refused with why, and the outcome says all, some or none. remove answers allocation_ids as rows to take away under `keep`, reopening exactly those targets once stored. position reads one row ({ row: { row_id, amount_field }, role, allocations: { list_id } }): its amount, applied, open and the allocations behind it. A row with no amount is refused: empty is not zero. Body: lists (the rows read), source { row_id, amount_field }, targets { list_id, amount_field, order_field?, row_ids? }, order, allocations { list_id?, *_field? }.",
    "input_schema": {
     "type": "object",
     "required": [
      "action",
      "list_id",
      "lists"
     ],
     "properties": {
      "action": {
       "type": "string",
       "enum": [
        "propose",
        "apply",
        "remove",
        "position"
       ]
      },
      "list_id": {
       "type": "string",
       "minLength": 1,
       "description": "The list in the request: the source (or the lines, or the row's list) when the body leaves its own list_id out."
      },
      "lists": {
       "type": "array",
       "items": {
        "type": "object"
       },
       "description": "The lists the action names, as the caller read them from a store: each { id, row_type, fields, ...the list's own definition, rows: [{ id, values }] } with every row the action reads. The run keeps nothing; what to store comes back as `keep`."
      }
     },
     "additionalProperties": true
    },
    "output_schema": {
